report.openIssues:
- The counter skips a block that one of the wallet's requests names, but nothing checks the other way round. If a short lead puts a request in a block one of the payer's own payments already names, the node refuses the request (409) or the payment lapses. §7.3 only asks for the counter to skip; refusing such a request would take about 3 lines in SignNameRequest.
- The wallet does not check R9 (a freeze, or a ⅔ freeze, that would leave no name seated). The node refuses it with 409, and the page shows the reason.
- The copy button uses navigator.clipboard, which browsers allow only in a secure context. localhost works, which is the default -listen address. A wallet opened by LAN IP over plain http cannot copy its full key, and a key change needs the new wallet's full key. A show-on-demand field would fix it, if the owner wants that.
- Drafts use the validator set the checkpoint carries (the set that signed the last block), as the code already did for votes. In dynamic mode it can differ from the set for the next block; the node checks again.
- With no verified state, the freeze relies on the unverified /hdls/status height and cannot see a pending change.
- Docs are S11's. ui/README.md and ui/USER_MANUAL.md must cover:
  - the Requests page and the desk;
  - the freeze button and "did not land";
  - the payment review that shows the payee's bank;
  - the address field;
  - hash names;
  - the new fields of <keyfile>.state (requestBlockIDs, lastName, newestHeight, freezeName, freezeBlockID);
  - lowercased names.
- Merge with S6: S9 uses only ledger.NameRequest, ledger.Reassignment, consensus.ValidatorSet and Vote/Commit, and node.Checkpoint/GovernanceView. If S6 changes any of those types, the ui tests need a small fix after the merge.

verdict.evidence:
The scratch copy <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S9-1 is an archive of p2-s9 HEAD 8c242ea. The worktree is clean, and git diff 5525c3b..HEAD changes only ui/*.go and ui/templates/*.html. All runs used GOTOOLCHAIN=auto (go1.27.3) and GOLEDGER_CHAOS_SLACK=4. Logs are in <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S9-logs/.

Static checks: gofmt -l . printed nothing outside review/. go vet ./... and go vet -C ui ./... are clean. go build ./... and go build -C ui -o /dev/null . pass.

Suites: go test -race -count=1 ./... passed twice (consensus 57 s and 54 s, node 61 s and 62 s, ledger, signing, cmd/server and cmd/demo ok). go test -C ui -race -count=1 ./... passed twice, in about 35 s each. The run with -count=3 -run 'Chaos|Restart|SignLog|Resume|CatchUp' ./node/ passed in 93 s. No time limit was changed.

Spec check: I compared each item of §7.1 to §7.7 and S9's scope in §10.2 with the code. Done:
- name status, with 'becomes yours' and the fingerprint plus copy button;
- the last name and newest height in <keyfile>.state, with an older state refused (also after a restart);
- the three warnings;
- the freeze: confirm step, height + lookahead or a sooner PendingHeight, the did-not-land report, and the last-name fallback;
- the Requests page: draft with a lead (default 120, max 3600), sign per role, submit;
- request blocks kept for the fee payer and skipped by the counter;
- the desk's pending list and its reminder;
- hash names: 15 bytes, lowercase base32, 26 characters;
- the payment review showing the payee's bank;
- the delegate, description and address form;
- the accounts table with fingerprints only;
- the admin parameter draft (ten parameters) and the name-action draft (every kind of action, new-key proof signed first, then votes);
- one checkpoint read per page.

I counted reads: every page, review and draft step, every sign step and every redirecting action reads the checkpoint once; the submit step for requests reads none. The deviations are reasonable readings: verified checkpoint passed in, payment review step, roles in the admin sign step, Sign refuses a freeze, desk scope, strings.ToLower. Nothing of S6, S10 or S11 is touched or half-built. Naming follows the rule, and I found no dead code or old-format path from this slice. Signed preimages go only through the existing ledger Sign* functions, and JSON round-trips of NameRequest and Reassignment keep every field. Every mutating route checks POST and sits behind guard; GET /requests never signs.

Mutations: I ran 41 of my own with <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S9-tools/mutate.py, mutations.json and mutations2.json. Each of the 16 tests the spec lists, and the builder's 7 extra tests, fails when its rule is reverted. Only M5c (request-block persistence) and M18b (an extra read in the Requests sign step) went uncaught; both are reported as test gaps. My first M19 mutation deadlocked, so I replaced it with a proper hold-across-status mutation, which the test catches.

Adversarial tests (<scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S9-3/ui/adversarial_test.go and counter_adversarial_test.go):
- a far-future BlockID is signed;
- the request-block skip runs past the window;
- a Kelvin-sign delegate is signed as 'kay' without being shown;
- a bogus admin proof gets a vote and its first-text placement blocks submission;
- a full key-change flow (holder, then new key, then bank) yields a complete, valid request;
- every action reads the checkpoint once.

All findings are minor; nothing is wrong at the consensus or signature level.
